Replace fixed sleeps in front of asynchronous state with bounded polling and
give the owner-signed roster and group-forwarding setup deterministic waits.

Group forwarding: the host learns that two members are directly connected
from their x.grp.mem.con messages; a late message overwrites the MRIntroduced
relation the test forces and forwarding is disabled, making the example time
out.  Wait until both relations are already MRConnected before forcing.

Promoted-members roster: the owner-signed roster snapshot and the owner intros
arrive asynchronously and have no terminal event, so poll the database for the
applied member role (checkMemberRowEventually) instead of relying on a fixed
sleep.  Negative checks stay immediate.

Also give the group-link member role / blocked name checks and the group
history disappearing-message TTL more time on a loaded builder.

